__pycache__/

# Generated, and two of these were committed by accident.
#
# `.coverage` is a SQLite database that embeds ABSOLUTE LOCAL PATHS -- the
# tracked copy contained 64 occurrences of the maintainer's home directory --
# and is not a portable report. `build/` held a stale second copy of io.py,
# leakproof/sweep.py and models/train.py that had drifted from src/aml,
# creating two apparent implementations for any reader or scanner.
#
# They are untracked now. They remain in history; see docs/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md,
# which treats that as a decision rather than a cleanup.
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
build/
dist/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.DS_Store
*.log

# HTML council reports are large generated artifacts; the transcripts are kept.
council-report-*.html

# Personal working notes: narrative learning material and superseded plans.
# Kept locally, not published. The technical record that IS published lives in
# aml-platform/paper/ (results), Cloud/ (architecture, cost, teardown) and
# AML_PROJECT_KNOWLEDGE.md (dataset facts the code comments cite).
Learning/
council-transcript-*.md

# NOTE, because this bit us: `Cloud/_v1_superseded/` used to be listed here.
# Those five files had already been committed in bfaa463, and ignoring a
# TRACKED file does not untrack it -- they were public the whole time. The
# entry read like a privacy control and was not one. They now live in
# docs/archive/Cloud/_v1_superseded/ and are deliberately published.
#
# If something must not be published, it must not be committed. A .gitignore
# entry added afterwards changes nothing.
